==English==

===Etymology===
Verb is from {{inh|en|enm|troublen}}, {{m|enm|trouble}}, borrowed from {{der|en|fro|troubler}}, {{m|fro|trobler}}, {{m|fro|trubler}}, metathetic variants of {{m|fro|tourbler}}, {{m|fro|torbler}}, {{m|fro|turbler}}, from {{der|en|la-vul|*turbulō}}, from {{der|en|la|turbula||disorderly group, a little crowd or people}}, diminutive of {{m|la|turba||stir; crowd}}. The noun is from {{inh|en|enm|trouble}}, {{m|enm|troble}}, from {{der|en|fro|troble}}, from the verb.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|trŭbʹəl}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈt͡ʃɹʌbəl/|/ˈtɹʌbəl/|a=RP,GA,CA}} ({{ipachar|/ʌ/}} and {{ipachar|/ə/}} are not actually different phonemes in North American English)
*** {{IPA|en|[ˈt͡ʃɹɐbɫ̩]|[ˈt̠͡ɹ̠̊˔ɐbɫ̩]|a=GA}}
**** {{audio|en|en-us-trouble.ogg|a=California}}
*** {{IPA|en|[ˈt͡ʃɹɜbɫ̩]|[ˈt̠͡ɹ̠̊˔ɜbɫ̩]|a=Southern US}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈtɹʊbəl/<!--|[ˈtɹʊbɫ̩]-->|a=Northern England}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈtɾʌbəl/<!--|[ˈtɾʌbɫ̩]-->|a=Scotland,Wales}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈtɹɐbəl/<!--|[ˈtɹɐbɫ̩]-->|a=AU,NZ}}
* {{hyphenation|en|trou|ble}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌbəl|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A [[distressing]] or [[dangerous]] [[situation]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:difficult situation}}
#: {{ux|en|He was in '''trouble''' when the rain started.}}
# A [[difficulty]], [[problem]], [[condition]], or [[action]] contributing to such a situation.
#: {{ux|en|The '''trouble''' was a leaking brake line.}}
#: {{ux|en|The bridge column magnified the '''trouble''' with a slight tilt in the wrong direction.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=XI|passage=Lest the fiend {{...}} some new '''trouble''' raise.|year=1873}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Macbeth|act=V|scene=i|passage=Foul whisperings are abroad; unnatural deeds / Do breed unnatural '''troubles'''.}}
# A [[person]] [[liable]] to [[place]] others or themselves in such a situation.
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Taylor Swift; w:Max Martin; {{w|Shellback (record producer)|Shellback}}|title={{w|I Knew You Were Trouble#"I Knew You Were Trouble (Taylor's Version)"|I Knew You Were '''Trouble''' (Taylor's Version)}}|album=w:Red (Taylor's Version)|year=2021|artist=Taylor Swift|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TqAollrUJdA|text=’Cause I knew you were '''trouble''' when you walked in<br>So shame on me no-ow}}
# The [[state]] of being [[troubled]], [[disturb]]ed, or [[distress]]ed [[mentally]]; [[unease]], [[disquiet]].
#: {{syn|en|anguish|torment|Thesaurus:distress}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XL|63|Yet oft when sundown skirts the moor<br>⁠An inner '''trouble''' I behold,<br>⁠A spectral doubt which makes me cold,<br>That I shall be thy mate no more, {{...}}}}
# [[objectionable|Objectionable]] [[feature]] of something or someone; [[problem]], [[drawback]], weakness, failing, or shortcoming.
#: {{syn|en|pain in the neck|Thesaurus:defect|Thesaurus:hindrance|Thesaurus:nuisance}}
#: {{ux|en|Your '''trouble''' is that you quit too readily.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''trouble''' with that suggestion is that we lack the funds to put it in motion.}}
# [[violent|Violent]] or [[turbulent]] [[occurrence]] or [[event]]; [[unrest]], [[disturbance]].
#: {{syn|en|palaver|turmoil|Thesaurus:commotion}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''troubles''' in Northern Ireland}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=7|passage=“I don’t know how you and the ‘head,’ as you call him, will get on, but I do know that if you call my duds a ‘livery’ again there’ll be '''trouble'''. It’s bad enough to go around togged out like a life saver on a drill day, but I can stand that ’cause I'm paid for it. What I won’t stand is to have them togs called a livery. {{...}}”}}
# [[effort|Effort]]s taken or [[expend]]ed, typically beyond the normal required.
#: {{ux|en|It’s no '''trouble''' for me to edit it.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1850|author=w:William Cullen Bryant|title=Letters of a Traveller
|passage=She never took the '''trouble''' to close them.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1881|author=s:Robert Louis Stevenson|title=s:Virginibus Puerisque
|passage=Indeed, by the report of our elders, this nervous preparation for old age is only '''trouble''' thrown away.}}
# [[difficulty|Difficulty]] in doing something.
#: {{ux|en|She has '''trouble''' eating.}}
# [[health|Health]] [[problem]]s, [[ailment]], generally of some particular part of the body.
#: {{syn|en|affliction|malady|Thesaurus:disease}}
#: {{ux|en|He’s been in hospital with some heart '''trouble'''.}}
# A [[malfunction]].
#: {{ux|en|My old car has engine '''trouble'''.}}
# {{cap|liability}} to [[punishment]]; [[conflict]] with [[authority]].
#: {{syn|en|grief|q1=informal}}
#: {{ux|en|He had some '''trouble''' with the law.}}
# {{lb|en|mining}} A [[fault]] or [[interruption]] in a [[stratum]].
# {{lb|en|Cockney rhyming slang}} {{U|wife}}. {{clipping of|en|trouble and strife}}.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:wife}}
# {{lb|en|slang|dated}} An [[unplanned]], [[unwanted]] or [[undesired]] [[pregnancy]].

