===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|now|rare}} To [[disturb]], [[stir up]], [[agitate]] (a medium, especially water).
#: {{syn|en|inturbidate|muddle|roil|stir}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|John|5|4|text=For an Angel went downe at a certaine season into the poole, and '''troubled''' the water:}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=X|line=1100|text=God looking forth will '''trouble''' all his Hoſt|year=1873}}
# {{senseid|en|to distress}}{{lb|en|transitive}} To [[mentally]] [[distress]]; to cause (someone) to be [[anxious]] or [[perplexed]].
#: {{syn|en|distress|torment|Thesaurus:vex}}
#: {{ux|en|What she said about narcissism is '''troubling''' me.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|John|12|27|text=Now is my soule '''troubled''', and what shall I say? Father, saue me from this houre, but for this cause came I vnto this houre.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Winter's Tale|II|i|281|2|passage=Take the Boy to you: he ſo '''troubles''' me, / ’Tis paſt enduring.}}
#* {{RQ:Locke Education|65|68|Never '''trouble''' your ſelf about thoſe Faults in them, which you know Age will cure.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} In weaker sense: to [[bother]] or [[inconvenience]].
#: {{syn|en|discommode|hassle|incommode|Thesaurus:annoy}}
#: {{ux|en|I will not '''trouble''' you to deliver the letter.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|of ailments, etc.}} To [[physically]] [[afflict]].
#: {{ux|en|My bad knee is '''troubling''' me.}}
# {{lb|en|reflexive|or|intransitive}} To [[take pains]] (to do something); to [[bother]].
#: {{syn|en|make an effort|take great pains}}
#: {{ux|en|I won’t '''trouble''' to post the letter today; I can do it tomorrow.}}
#* {{RQ:Lawrence Lady Chatterley's Lover|10|132|«&thinsp;The hut’s not very tidy, if you don’t mind,&thinsp;» he said. «&thinsp;I cleared it what I could.&thinsp;» / «&thinsp;But I didn’t want you to '''trouble'''!&thinsp;» she said.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[worry]]; to be anxious.
#: {{syn|en|angst|anxietize|cark|fret}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1946|author=w:Bertrand Russell|title=History of Western Philosophy|section=I.26
|passage=Why '''trouble''' about the future? It is wholly uncertain.}}

